              "quote": "By chance a certain priest was going down that way.",
              "unit": "luke-10-31"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Priest in the Samaritan parable: a man of middle years with a lean, weathered build and dark, short-cropped hair and a close-trimmed beard streaked with grey. Sun-browned skin and a serious, careful face. He wears a long priestly robe of undyed linen with a dark woven sash and a fringed prayer shawl over the shoulders, in muted ochre and off-white. He carries nothing in his hands but a small leather scrip at his side."
